<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Turkish War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1683–1699</span> · Also known as War of the Holy League</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Turkish War was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-league-1684">Holy League</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> from 1683 to 1699. It began with the failed Ottoman siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> and saw the Habsburgs conquer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> while Venice took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morean-war">Morean War</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> of 1699 confirmed the first major Ottoman territorial losses in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-turkish-war.jpg" alt="Great Turkish War" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DavidDijkgraaf · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Turkish_War_Collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
